From 88dd9c06d840374610d23b1163529324312cb08f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BellSoft <info@bell-sw.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:08:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vendordb): serve the vendor distributions and runtimes
 from its OSV data

Local (vendor-specific) change, applied after the upstream series.

Add grype/vulnerability/vendordb, a vulnerability.Provider wrapping the
provider of grype.LoadVulnerabilityDB: queries for the vendor distro
namespaces and for the vendor JDK / NIK package types are answered from the
OSV bulk archives the vendor publishes (<base>/<ecosystem>/all.zip),
everything else by Anchore's database; `grype db` is untouched.

Archive download, cache (24 h TTL, compact index), apk / JDK / NIK range
evaluation and the origin -> provides alias resolution are the shared
osv-internal module's (github.com/bell-sw/osv-internal); the adapter routes
criteria, builds grype vulnerabilities (CVE as id, BELL-CVE id as advisory
and related vulnerability, fix state, severity from the CVSS vector, record
URL as data source) and enriches the metadata from the wrapped database by
CVE id (NVD CVSS, EPSS, KEV, CWEs).

Configuration follows the scheme shared by every scanner with vendor
support: --vendor-url / GRYPE_VENDOR_URL / vendor.url (base location for
all products), --vendor-feed "<product>=<url>" (repeatable) /
GRYPE_VENDOR_FEED (comma-separated) / vendor.feed (list or map),
--vendor-strict / GRYPE_VENDOR_STRICT / vendor.strict; precedence feed >
url > built-in source (the osv.dev bucket for the distributions, the
module's product base URL for the standalone runtimes). Grype-specific:
vendor.{enabled,cache-dir,cache-ttl,download-timeout}.

The distro types, the IDMapping keys, the ecosystems of the OSV transformer
and the namespace prefix (vendordb.Provider) take their values from
osv-internal, as do the tests.

When the archive of a family cannot be obtained (download failure, HTTP
error, db.auto-update=false with nothing cached) the scan prints the
module's canonical warning once per family, at WARN level and as a closing
notification, and continues without that family's findings; the exit code
is not affected. With --vendor-strict the scan fails instead.

The apk matcher does not consult NVD's CPE records for the packages of
these two distributions, like trivy and osv-scanner: grype's NVD fallback
exists for Alpine's secdb, which lists fixed CVEs only, while the vendor
feed carries affected ranges with and without a fix. Other apk
distributions keep the stock behaviour.

go.mod requires github.com/bell-sw/osv-internal v0.5.0. The module is
private; the build replaces the import path with the module source
installed by the osv-internal package (see the APKBUILD).
